Under known-zero-mean Gaussian sampling, if \(D=\lambda_0\Delta_1^a\Delta_2^b\delta^e\) is a three-level nested flag power and \(m=(a+b+e,b+e,e)\), then
\[
 \frac{D(\widehat\Sigma)}{D(\Sigma)}
 \stackrel{d}{=}
 \prod_{j=1}^{3}
 \left(\frac{\chi^2_{n-j+1}}{n}\right)^{m_j},
\]
with independent chi-squared factors.
